From: Lucas C.S. <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] components/private_verification_tokens: reach ATHM through a cxx bridge, not Crubit

M154 (upstream 4ff7d01fb98f, "[PVT] Migrate athm_ffi to use Crubit instead
of cxx") moved the ATHM bindings to a Crubit `cpp_api_from_rust` binding.
`cpp_api_from_rust` only exists when `enable_cpp_api_from_rust` is true,
and //build/config/rust.gni turns it false whenever `rust_sysroot_absolute`
is set, so with a system Rust sysroot gn never defines `athm_ffi_bindings`
and `gn gen` dies:

  ERROR Unresolved dependencies.
  //components/private_verification_tokens/common:privacy_pass_athm_batch_request(...)
    needs //components/private_verification_tokens/common/athm_ffi:athm_ffi_bindings(...)

This cannot be a revert: //chrome/browser/private_verification_tokens
consumes the API, and M155 rewrote the client side on top of the Crubit
binding (AthmParameters/AthmClientRequest gave way to a single
PrivacyPassBatchClient that builds the whole request body and finalizes the
whole batch).  So the Rust crate is kept exactly as upstream ships it, and
only the binding layer is swapped:

 - athm_ffi/athm_cxx.rs (new) is a `cxx` bridge over PrivacyPassBatchClient,
   the one type PrivacyPassAthmBatchRequest uses.  `cxx` cannot return a
   `Result` without C++ exceptions, so a failed constructor yields an object
   whose `batch_client_ok()` is false, and `finalize` returns a shared enum
   that keeps upstream's InvalidInput/OperationFailed distinction.  `cxx`
   has no Vec<Vec<u8>>, so the finalized tokens come back concatenated
   with their lengths alongside.
 - privacy_pass_athm_batch_request.{h,cc} hold a `rust::Box` of the bridge
   type instead of the Crubit one, and pass slices through
   base::SpanToRustSlice.  Behaviour and error mapping are unchanged.
 - The test-only targets (common:test_support, the batch request unittest,
   and chrome/browser's unit_tests and browser_tests) drive the *issuer*
   half through Crubit -- private_verification_tokens_test_util.h hands out
   a PrivacyPassAthmIssuer.  They keep their definitions, so every reference
   to them still resolves, but their `athm_ffi_bindings` dependency is gated
   on `enable_cpp_api_from_rust`: with a system sysroot they are defined
   and not buildable, which costs nothing here since the ebuild only builds
   base_unittests.

Same reachability as chromium-155-blink-fonts-cxx-not-crubit.patch: applied
only with USE=-bundled-toolchain.  Drop this patch once the overlay builds
Crubit for the system toolchain, or upstream gates the dependency on
`enable_cpp_api_from_rust`.
